  "full_text": "Look at the first-person shooter in the Flight Simulator. The Flight Simulator is called Eagle Dive. You're an eagle looking for fish, and there's boats in the river. Okay, I got a fish. Another fish. So let's look at the source code. Demo Games Directory. It has graphics and source. Here's the sprites. There's the big boat. the fish is right there the tree is the green thing it's a really large because they get shrunk anyway so it's done with multi-core and each core does a strip of terrain and it starts at the center and alternates outward they try and stay out of each other's way so let's look at the first-person shooter. God said they were dancing. Some distortion. So it has graphics and source. There's sprites. This is done with one core, and it's not very many lines of code, and that's the point. There's the map. I went ahead and did it as a sprite, and you can change the map. You have a map editor just changing the sprite. So if we wanted to align so just doing that will change that",
